:name: HWA10 update-run fixups
:description: The addresses the update run hooks in the application image, and
:  what it re-applies once the bootloader has overwritten internal flash with
:  the bank. A layout that moves the text has them elsewhere, so this file is
:  what abi/sim_patches.py rewrites; update-test.resc includes it after
:  machine.resc, and the redefined imagePatches therefore applies to the image
:  the update installed, not to the one the run started from.

# The application's reset entry, which the bootloader jumps to. It is the one
# address here that belongs to the image the update installs rather than to the
# one the run started from, which is why it is the only one rewritten alongside
# the fixups themselves.
$appReset?=0x34938
# The three application addresses the WPP pipe hooks (hwa10.repl gives it the
# ones the image it was parsed with had).
$wppPresent?=0x37370
$wppPoll?=0x3739c
$wppHvx?=0x935b4

macro postUpdate
"""
    runMacro $imagePatches
    sysbus.wppPipe Rehook $wppPresent $wppPoll $wppHvx
    # main init sleeps vTaskDelay(30001) before bringing up the UI (`movw r0,
    # #0x7531`); make that 2001 ticks so the link is usable sooner.
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x91faa 0x70D1F240
    # 0x20000000 is where the MBR keeps the vector table it forwards SVCs and
    # interrupts to. Launching the bootloader pointed it at the bootloader's own
    # table and the bootloader jumps to the application without putting it back,
    # so the first SVC -- the one that starts the FreeRTOS scheduler -- lands in
    # the bootloader and the application never runs a task. Point it at the
    # SoftDevice, which is what the MBR leaves behind when it starts the
    # SoftDevice itself.
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20000000 0x1000
    sysbus.nvmc SnapshotProtectedRegion 0x0 0x27000
    sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x10001014 0xFFFFFFFF
"""
